{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-116973",
  "enisaUuid": "d51c71d8-d0ad-3749-947f-d5ac84ab0a63",
  "description": "A vulnerability in the authorization mechanism of Cisco Identity Services Engine (ISE) and Cisco ISE Passive Identity Connector (ISE-PIC) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to obtain an endpoint identity certificate.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to improper authorization checks. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted request to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to bypass authorization to obtain an endpoint certificate.",
